.TH PLYCOUNT 1 "October 2026" "plycount 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plycount \- add, update, or verify PlyCount tags in PGN chess databases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plycount
[\fIoptions\fR]
.I INPUT OUTPUT
.br
.B plycount --verify
[\fIoptions\fR]
.I INPUT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B plycount
is a command-line utility for chess games stored in Portable Game Notation
(PGN) files and databases. It adds or updates the \fBPlyCount\fR tag for each
selected game and can verify existing tags. It streams the PGN input, so large
chess databases can be processed without loading the complete collection into
memory. The input is never modified in place.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --verify
Check \fBPlyCount\fR tags instead of writing an output file. Verification
continues after ordinary tag discrepancies.
.TP
.B --limit N
Process only the first \fIN\fR games encountered. \fIN\fR must be a positive
decimal integer. In rewrite mode, only these games are written; in verify mode,
only these games are checked.
.TP
.B --force
Allow an existing output path to be replaced after successful processing.
This option is valid only in rewrite mode.
.TP
.B --version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.B --help, -h, -?
Print usage information and exit.
.SH "PLYCOUNT SEMANTICS"
The count is the number of plies in the main line of a chess game as present in
the PGN record's movetext. One move by one player is one ply. Recursive
annotation variations (RAVs), comments, numeric or symbolic NAGs, move numbers,
and game-result tokens are not counted. A FEN fullmove number is not added to
the count.
.PP
The program counts movetext tokens; it does not validate SAN or the legality
of chess moves, and does not replay moves against a chess position.
.SH "VERIFY MODE"
Verify mode checks every selected game even when earlier games have
discrepancies. A game is classified as correct, missing, mismatched, invalid,
or duplicate. Duplicate tags are reported as the duplicate category.
.PP
At most 100 individual discrepancy diagnostics are printed. Further per-game
diagnostics are suppressed, but checking continues, all category counters are
maintained, and the final summary includes all selected games.
.SH "OUTPUT SAFETY"
\fIINPUT\fR and \fIOUTPUT\fR must not identify the same file. Existing files are
checked using file identity and resolved paths. An existing output is refused
unless \fB--force\fR is specified. The input is opened read-only.
.PP
Rewrite output is first written to a uniquely created temporary file in the
output directory. After processing and closing the stage successfully, it is
renamed to \fIOUTPUT\fR. A failed run does not publish the staged output.
.SH PROGRESS
Long runs may report progress to standard error. Progress is throttled; its
frequency is not a fixed interface guarantee.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Processing succeeded, or verification completed with no discrepancies.
.TP
.B 1
Verification completed but found one or more \fBPlyCount\fR discrepancies.
.TP
.B 2
Invocation error or fatal processing error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Add or update counts in a PGN chess database:
.PP
.nf
plycount games.pgn games-counted.pgn
.fi
.PP
Verify a PGN chess database:
.PP
.nf
plycount --verify games-counted.pgn
.fi
.PP
Process only the first 500 games:
.PP
.nf
plycount --limit 500 games.pgn first-500.pgn
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
A single PGN game is limited to 64 MiB in memory. Game boundaries are detected
from PGN record structure; the program does not perform full PGN grammar or SAN
legality validation. Output publication can fail if the output directory does
not permit temporary-file creation or rename.
